# Build-context hygiene.
#
# Dockerfile.web runs `npm ci` and then `COPY . .`. Without this file the host's
# node_modules, .next and .git land on top of the image's freshly installed
# dependencies, which breaks native binaries (for example the platform-specific
# @next/swc package when the host is macOS and the image is Linux) and inflates
# the build context.
.git
.github
.gitignore
node_modules
.next
out
coverage
.vercel
.venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
*.db
*.db-journal
data
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
docs
tests
.scratch
*.log
